# Build context for guardmatch-web.
#
# The context is this directory. Everything at the repository root — docs/, the
# backend, the task runners, PLAN.md and PROGRESS.md — is already outside it, and
# is not listed here: a rule for a path that cannot exist reads as protection and
# gives none.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Present, and deliberately excluded
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json. A host node_modules holds
# platform-specific binaries — the wrong esbuild and the wrong sharp — and is by
# far the largest thing in this directory.
node_modules/

# Rebuilt by `npm run build` in the builder stage. Copying a host build in would
# let a stale bundle silently win over a fresh compile.
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Run by CI and by `npm test`, never inside the image.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
vitest.config.ts

# Not read at runtime, and read by the builder before the context is sent.
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absent today, and must stay absent — kept precisely because they match nothing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next.js inlines any NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable into the client bundle at build time.
# A local .env reaching this context would therefore not merely sit in a layer —
# it could be compiled into JavaScript served to every visitor.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
